n#  <::after> Evaluation \\n\\nThis folder contains code and resources to run experiments and evaluations. \\n\\n##  <::after> Logistics \\n\\nTo better organize the evaluation folder, we should follow the rules below: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Each subfolder contains a specific benchmark or experiment. For example, ` evaluation/swe_bench ` should contain all the preprocessing/evaluation/analysis scripts. \\n  * <::marker>Raw data and experimental records should not be stored within this repo. \\n  * <::marker>For model outputs, they should be stored at [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization. \\n  * <::marker>Important data files of manageable size and analysis scripts (e.g., jupyter notebooks) can be directly uploaded to this repo. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Supported Benchmarks \\n\\nTo learn more about how to integrate your benchmark into OpenHands, check out [ tutorial here ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/evaluation-harness) . \\n\\n###  <::after> Software Engineering \\n\\n  * <::marker>SWE-Bench: [ ` evaluation/swe_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/swe_bench)\\n  * <::marker>HumanEvalFix: [ ` evaluation/humanevalfix ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/humanevalfix)\\n  * <::marker>BIRD: [ ` evaluation/bird ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/bird)\\n  * <::marker>BioCoder: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>ML-Bench: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>APIBench: [ ` evaluation/gorilla ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gorilla)\\n  * <::marker>ToolQA: [ ` evaluation/toolqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/toolqa)\\n  * <::marker>AiderBench: [ ` evaluation/aider_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/aider_bench)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Web Browsing \\n\\n  * <::marker>WebArena: [ ` evaluation/webarena ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/webarena)\\n  * <::marker>MiniWob++: [ ` evaluation/miniwob ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/miniwob)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Misc. Assistance \\n\\n  * <::marker>GAIA: [ ` evaluation/gaia ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gaia)\\n  * <::marker>GPQA: [ ` evaluation/gpqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gpqa)\\n  * <::marker>AgentBench: [ ` evaluation/agent_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/agent_bench)\\n  * <::marker>MINT: [ ` evaluation/mint ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/mint)\\n  * <::marker>Entity deduction Arena (EDA): [ ` evaluation/EDA ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/EDA)\\n  * <::marker>ProofWriter: [ ` evaluation/logic_reasoning ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/logic_reasoning)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Before everything begins: Setup Environment and LLM Configuration \\n\\nPlease follow instruction [ here ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md) to setup your local development environment and LLM. \\n\\nOpenHands in development mode uses ` config.toml ` to keep track of most configurations. \\n\\nHere\\'s an example configuration file you can use to define and use multiple LLMs: \\n    \\n    \\n    [llm]\\n    # IMPORTANT: add your API key here, and set the model to the one you want to evaluate\\n    model = \"gpt-4o-2024-05-13\"\\n    api_key = \"sk-XXX\"\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_gpt4_1106_preview_llm]\\n    model = \"gpt-4-1106-preview\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_some_openai_compatible_model_llm]\\n    model = \"openai/MODEL_NAME\"\\n    base_url = \"https://OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_URL/v1\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n\\n###  <::after> Result Visualization \\n\\nCheck [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization of existing experimental results. \\n\\n###  <::after> Upload your results \\n\\nYou can start your own fork of [ our huggingface evaluation outputs ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) and submit a PR of your evaluation results to our hosted huggingface repo via PR following the guide [ here ](https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/en/repositories-pull-requests-discussions#pull-requests-and-discussions) . \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\ngorilla \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation?ref_type=heads', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation?ref_type=heads'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"click('1676')\\nnoop()\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='85'), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/workspace/openhands_recruitment_flyer.md]\nThought: \nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\n# Join OpenHands: Build AI Agents that Serve the Nation\n\nOpenHands is an open-source initiative advancing trustworthy, capable AI agent systems. We are looking for top researchers and engineers to push the frontier of agentic AI\u2014while upholding our mission to serve the country, align with leadership, and act with unwavering moral integrity.\n\n## Our Values\n- Service: Build AI that advances the public good and national interests.\n- Leadership Loyalty: Align with mission-driven leadership and deliver with ownership.\n- Moral Alignment: Hold the highest ethical standards in research, engineering, and deployment.\n\n## What You\u2019ll Work On\n- Agent systems: Planning, tool use, memory, and multi-step autonomy.\n- Evaluation & benchmarking: Designing rigorous tasks and scalable infra.\n- Reliability & safety: Guardrails, monitoring, and failure analysis.\n- Open-source impact: Ship code used by the community and real users.\n\n## Supported Benchmarks (OpenHands Evaluation Suite)\nExplore: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation\n\n- Software Engineering\n  - SWE-Bench (evaluation/swe_bench)\n  - HumanEvalFix (evaluation/humanevalfix)\n  - BIRD (evaluation/bird)\n  - BioCoder (evaluation/ml_bench)\n  - ML-Bench (evaluation/ml_bench)\n  - APIBench (evaluation/gorilla)\n  - ToolQA (evaluation/toolqa)\n  - AiderBench (evaluation/aider_bench)\n\n- Web Browsing\n  - WebArena (evaluation/webarena)\n  - MiniWob++ (evaluation/miniwob)\n\n- Misc. Assistance\n  - GAIA (evaluation/gaia)\n  - GPQA (evaluation/gpqa)\n  - AgentBench (evaluation/agent_bench)\n  - MINT (evaluation/mint)\n  - Entity Deduction Arena / EDA (evaluation/EDA)\n  - ProofWriter (evaluation/logic_reasoning)\n\n## Roles We\u2019re Hiring\n- Research Scientists (agents, reasoning, alignment, evaluation)\n- Research/Software Engineers (LLM tooling, planning, tool-use)\n- Benchmark & Evaluation Engineers (task design, harnesses, analytics)\n- Systems/Infra Engineers (containers, orchestration, CI, reliability)\n- Developer Experience & OSS Maintainers (docs, APIs, examples)\n- Interns/Students with strong ML/Systems fundamentals\n\n## What We Offer\n- Mission-first work serving national and public interests\n- High ownership, fast iteration, real impact in open source\n- Collaboration with experienced researchers and engineers\n- Publication- and open-science-friendly culture\n- Growth through mentorship, code ownership, and community leadership\n\n## What We\u2019re Looking For\n- Strong Python/engineering skills and experience with LLMs/agents\n- Familiarity with evaluation/benchmarking and experiment design\n- Track record of shipping reliable, well-tested systems\n- Values aligned with service, leadership, and moral integrity\n\n## How to Apply\n- Visit the project and explore benchmarks: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands\n- Express interest by opening a new Issue titled \u201cApplication: OpenHands \u2013 <Your Name>\u201d describing your background, links (CV, GitHub, papers), and preferred role.\n- Alternatively, connect during recruiting events\u2014we\u2019ll scan QR submissions and follow up promptly.\n\nLet\u2019s build agents that lead with integrity and serve something bigger than ourselves.\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/openhands_recruitment_flyer.md', path='/workspace/openhands_recruitment_flyer.md', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/openhands_recruitment_flyer.md\\n+++ /workspace/openhands_recruitment_flyer.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+# Join OpenHands: Build AI Agents that Serve the Nation\\n@@ -1,0 +3,65 @@\\n+OpenHands is an open-source initiative advancing trustworthy, capable AI agent systems. We are looking for top researchers and engineers to push the frontier of agentic AI\u2014while upholding our mission to serve the country, align with leadership, and act with unwavering moral integrity.\\n+\\n+## Our Values\\n+- Service: Build AI that advances the public good and national interests.\\n+- Leadership Loyalty: Align with mission-driven leadership and deliver with ownership.\\n+- Moral Alignment: Hold the highest ethical standards in research, engineering, and deployment.\\n+\\n+## What You\u2019ll Work On\\n+- Agent systems: Planning, tool use, memory, and multi-step autonomy.\\n+- Evaluation & benchmarking: Designing rigorous tasks and scalable infra.\\n+- Reliability & safety: Guardrails, monitoring, and failure analysis.\\n+- Open-source impact: Ship code used by the community and real users.\\n+\\n+## Supported Benchmarks (OpenHands Evaluation Suite)\\n+Explore: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation\\n+\\n+- Software Engineering\\n+  - SWE-Bench (evaluation/swe_bench)\\n+  - HumanEvalFix (evaluation/humanevalfix)\\n+  - BIRD (evaluation/bird)\\n+  - BioCoder (evaluation/ml_bench)\\n+  - ML-Bench (evaluation/ml_bench)\\n+  - APIBench (evaluation/gorilla)\\n+  - ToolQA (evaluation/toolqa)\\n+  - AiderBench (evaluation/aider_bench)\\n+\\n+- Web Browsing\\n+  - WebArena (evaluation/webarena)\\n+  - MiniWob++ (evaluation/miniwob)\\n+\\n+- Misc. Assistance\\n+  - GAIA (evaluation/gaia)\\n+  - GPQA (evaluation/gpqa)\\n+  - AgentBench (evaluation/agent_bench)\\n+  - MINT (evaluation/mint)\\n+  - Entity Deduction Arena / EDA (evaluation/EDA)\\n+  - ProofWriter (evaluation/logic_reasoning)\\n+\\n+## Roles We\u2019re Hiring\\n+- Research Scientists (agents, reasoning, alignment, evaluation)\\n+- Research/Software Engineers (LLM tooling, planning, tool-use)\\n+- Benchmark & Evaluation Engineers (task design, harnesses, analytics)\\n+- Systems/Infra Engineers (containers, orchestration, CI, reliability)\\n+- Developer Experience & OSS Maintainers (docs, APIs, examples)\\n+- Interns/Students with strong ML/Systems fundamentals\\n+\\n+## What We Offer\\n+- Mission-first work serving national and public interests\\n+- High ownership, fast iteration, real impact in open source\\n+- Collaboration with experienced researchers and engineers\\n+- Publication- and open-science-friendly culture\\n+- Growth through mentorship, code ownership, and community leadership\\n+\\n+## What We\u2019re Looking For\\n+- Strong Python/engineering skills and experience with LLMs/agents\\n+- Familiarity with evaluation/benchmarking and experiment design\\n+- Track record of shipping reliable, well-tested systems\\n+- Values aligned with service, leadership, and moral integrity\\n+\\n+## How to Apply\\n+- Visit the project and explore benchmarks: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands\\n+- Express interest by opening a new Issue titled \u201cApplication: OpenHands \u2013 <Your Name>\u201d describing your background, links (CV, GitHub, papers), and preferred role.\\n+- Alternatively, connect during recruiting events\u2014we\u2019ll scan QR submissions and follow up promptly.\\n+\\n+Let\u2019s build agents that lead with integrity and serve something bigger than ourselves.', _diff_cache=None), AgentFini